    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0433" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1750.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Johnson to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 200.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 26, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with your telegraphic
                    instruction dated July 27, 5 p.m., I have the honor to send enclosed herein the
                    Legation’s recommendations upon the subject of the., liquidation of diversions
                    of revenue by the Dominican Government due to its extraordinary expenses since
                    July 7, 1915, in attempting to suppress minor uprisings that have occurred; and
                    upon the subject of the reestablishment of the Government’s finances on a sound
                    basis, once order is restored. As the enclosed report deals only with current
                    obligations a later supplemental report will be sent on the subject of the
                    unpaid claims against the Dominican Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart Johnson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d314-a1.xml" xpointer="d314-a1"/>
            </div>
